  "changelog": "v159: documentation trueing for the Conversation Interaction (issue #121, wave 4 \u2014 the closer). README and docs describe the conversation flow now that it's shipped, not the contract-era placeholder text. All nine README.md mermaid diagrams audited; three redrawn (the big-picture flowchart now shows the conversation turn engine, the session document, and the extracted-outputs fan-out at close instead of the stale \"warm ack \u00b7 optional follow-up\" node; the daily-loop sequence diagram shows the arc-card attach step and the real save-then-turn order, with the old \"ships in the next waves\" note removed now that it has shipped; the three-clocks diagram gains WEEKLY's arc-planning step and ON ANSWER's session-open/turn/close-with-coalesced-compile-and-commit shape) plus two more updated in place (the planner flowchart gains the engagement-profile input and the arc-card attach point; the candidate-lifecycle flowchart gains the `conversation` source). Core-concepts table gains Chat/Conversation/Arc card/Session rows; script tables gain conversation.py/conversation_delivery.py/conversation_lints.py/arc_planner.py/interaction_evals.py and true process_answer.py/ingest_story.py/daily_question.sh/weekly_maintenance.sh/monthly_research.sh/jobs.py/question_planner.py against shipped behavior (including the previously-undocumented monthly `arc-thread-offers` step \u2014 the \"a thread the system offered\" half of the Conversation definition). Key commands gains route/conversation-status/conversation-close/conversation-evals/arc-plan/arc-thread-offers. README.template.md's Nomenclature/Schedule/Loop sections get the same trueing so new vaults are born current. CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md's Unprompted Story Ingest sections now describe the issue #117 immediate Conversation turn (skill/SKILL.md already did); CLAUDE.md's Processing-an-Answer section corrected on two points found during the walk: the per-answer wiki compile is conditional on session state (not unconditional), and the chat/phone-path wrapper's duplicate-notice suppression does not recognize a successful conversation turn \u2014 a real v153-era regression, filed as lifehug#133 and documented as shipped (buggy) behavior rather than silently patched or silently glossed over, per this PR's own scope rule. CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/skill/SKILL.md's five-intent router prose, research.md \u00a711's pointer, and all four conversation ADRs' Consequences were audited and verified already true against shipped code \u2014 no changes needed there. Full doc-audit evidence table (every diagram element-group and touched-section claim, verdict VERIFIED/FIXED, zero unfixed STALE rows) posted on PR #129.",
